      "problem": "What number is $175%$ greater than $48?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find a number $175%$ *greater than* $48,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+175%=275%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n275%=\\frac{275}{100}=2.75\n$$\n\nSo, to find a number that is $175%$ greater than $48,$ we multiply $48$ by $2.75:$\n\n$$\n2.75\\cdot 48=132\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number that is $175%$ greater than $48$ is $132.$",
